      en: 'In the Rajbati quarter on the north-eastern edge of Dinajpur town stand the remains of the palace complex of the Dinajpur Raj — the same royal family that built Kantajew Temple and dug Ramsagar. The main buildings are thought to date largely from the 18th century, with later additions, and the complex was badly damaged in the earthquake of 1897.\n\nThe compound once held a mirror palace (Ayna Mahal), a queen’s palace, a family shrine and several temples. Today most of it is a ruin of peeling plaster, roots gripping brick walls and empty doorways, though the temple within the compound is still in use for worship.\n\nThis is a place for history lovers rather than a polished attraction. On a misty winter morning the faded grandeur is at its most atmospheric, and the walk round the ruins takes about an hour.',
