      en: 'The Friendship Centre at Kashdaha, on the outskirts of Gaibandha, is a training campus of the development organisation Friendship — and a pilgrimage site for architecture enthusiasts. Designed by Kashef Mahboob Chowdhury of URBANA, it won the Aga Khan Award for Architecture in 2016.\n\nBuilt on flood-prone land inside a protective embankment, the complex sits low, its grass-covered roofs almost level with the ground. Inside is a sequence of hand-made brick walls, sunken courtyards, pools and carefully framed light, a plan said to draw on the layout of ancient Buddhist monasteries such as those at Mahasthangarh.\n\nIt is a working institution rather than a tourist attraction, so visits are only possible with prior permission. In the monsoon, when the pools are full, the reflections on the brick walls are at their most beautiful.',
