      en: 'In Nidaria village of Lalmonirhat Sadar, this 18th-century three-domed Mughal-style mosque is among the oldest buildings in the district. Its inscription is said to place it in the mid-18th century, though accounts of who built it differ.\n\nThree domes sit over the rectangular prayer hall, with octagonal turrets at the corners and recessed panels and floral motifs on the walls. It is small, but its proportions and ornament carry the elegance of Mughal architecture.\n\nIts setting among green paddy fields and trees adds to the charm. Daily prayers are still held here, so visit between prayer times for an unhurried look at the details.',
