      en: 'In Balia village near Bhulli in Thakurgaon Sadar, the three-domed Balia Mosque is popularly known as the “Mosque of the Jinn”. Construction is said to have begun in the late 19th century under a local zamindar family, but for various reasons the domes were never completed at the time. Legend says jinn built it in a single night, which is where the nickname comes from.\n\nAfter standing unfinished and decaying for many years, it was restored in the 21st century and its domes were added. With a high plinth, arches, minarets and lime-plaster detailing in the Mughal manner, the mosque shines once more.\n\nToday it is one of the most visited monuments in Thakurgaon and a working place of prayer. Visit between prayer times to take in the architecture calmly.',
